The `DiskANNIndex` class is in `src/vector/diskann_index.h` (provided):

```cpp
class DiskANNIndex {
public:
    DiskANNIndex(uint32_t max_degree = 32, uint32_t beam_width = 64);
    void Build(const vector<Vector>& vectors);       // YOU IMPLEMENT
    vector<pair<uint32_t, float>> Search(             // YOU IMPLEMENT
        const Vector& query, uint32_t k);
    void RobustPrune(uint32_t node_id,                // YOU IMPLEMENT
        vector<pair<uint32_t, float>>& candidates);
private:
    uint32_t max_degree_;   // R: max neighbors per node
    uint32_t beam_width_;   // L: search beam width
    uint32_t entry_point_;  // starting node for search
    vector<Vector> vectors_;              // all indexed vectors
    vector<vector<uint32_t>> adjacency_;  // neighbor lists
};
```

**Also implement `L2Distance` (the fundamental metric):**

functions.description:
Greedy beam search starting from `entry_point_`.

```
candidates = {entry_point}
visited = {}
result = [] (sorted by distance, max size = beam_width_)

while candidates has unvisited nodes:
    p = closest unvisited in candidates
    mark p visited
    if p farther than result[L-1]: skip
    for each neighbor n of p:
        d = L2Distance(query, vectors[n])
        if d < result.back() or |result| < L:
            add (d, n) to candidates and result
            sort result, trim to L
return first K entries of result
```

